# Branching

Trunk-based development. `staging` is the trunk and the GitHub default branch. Open pull requests against `staging`.

`main` is the release line. The Release action tags it, and it lags `staging`. Do not start feature work from `main`.

`pnpm worktree:new` creates the branch from the current commit, so run it from an up-to-date `staging`:

```bash
git fetch origin staging
git checkout staging
git pull
pnpm worktree:new -- feat/short-name
cd ../degage-feat-short-name
pnpm dev
```

The `--` is required. The sibling folder is `<repo-directory>-<branch>` with `/` turned into `-`. From this checkout that is `../degage-feat-short-name`.

Details: `docs/en/local-development.md`.
